The ultimate party appetizer or casual dinner crowd-pleaser. Homemade tender ground beef meatballs are baked to golden brown, then simmered in a vibrant sweet-and-tangy glaze made from cranberry sauce, your favorite barbecue sauce, and a touch of sweet chili.

*Adapted from [Delish](https://www.delish.com/cooking/recipe-ideas/a23694828/cocktail-meatballs/).*

## Ingredients

### Meatballs
- 1 lb lean ground beef (85% or 90% lean)
- 2 large eggs, lightly beaten
- ½ cup plain breadcrumbs (or panko)
- ¼ medium yellow onion, finely minced
- ¼ cup finely chopped fresh flat-leaf parsley (plus extra for garnish)
- 1 teaspoon kosher salt
- ½ teaspoon freshly cracked black pepper

### Sweet and Tangy Glaze
- 1 can (14 oz) cranberry sauce (jellied or whole berry)
- 1 cup barbecue sauce
- ½ cup sweet chili sauce
- 2 tablespoons apple cider vinegar
- 1 tablespoon Worcestershire sauce
- 1 pinch crushed red pepper flakes
- Kosher salt, to taste

## Instructions

1. **Preheat and Prep the Pan:** Heat oven to 350°F (175°C). Line a large rimmed baking sheet with parchment paper or foil for hassle-free cleanup.
2. **Combine the Meatball Base:** In a large bowl, combine the ground beef, beaten eggs, breadcrumbs, minced yellow onion, and chopped fresh parsley. Season with the kosher salt and freshly cracked black pepper. Use your hands or a fork to gently combine until the ingredients are distributed; avoid over-mixing so the meatballs stay tender.
3. **Shape into Rounds:** Roll the mixture into 16 uniform spheres, approximately 1 ½ inches in diameter. Place them evenly spaced on the prepared baking sheet.
4. **Bake and Turn:** Slide into the oven and bake for 10 minutes. Use tongs to flip each meatball over, then bake for an additional 10 minutes until cooked through and lightly golden on the outside.
5. **Whisk the Cocktail Glaze:** While the meatballs are in the oven, place a large wide skillet over medium heat. Add the cranberry sauce, barbecue sauce, sweet chili sauce, apple cider vinegar, Worcestershire sauce, crushed red pepper flakes, and a small pinch of salt. Whisk vigorously until the cranberry sauce breaks down and the sauce turns smooth and glossy.
6. **Simmer and Coat:** Add the hot baked meatballs directly into the bubbling glaze. Reduce heat to medium-low and simmer for about 5 minutes, gently stirring and basting with a spoon so the sauce reduces and forms a thick, sticky coating around every meatball.
7. **Plate and Garnish:** Transfer the meatballs and remaining pan glaze to a warm serving bowl or platter. Sprinkle with freshly chopped parsley and serve warm with cocktail toothpicks.

## Notes

- **Slow Cooker Friendly:** For game days and potlucks, place the baked meatballs straight into a 4-to-6-quart slow cooker. Pour the whisked sauce over them and heat on LOW for 2 to 3 hours, keeping on the WARM setting throughout the event.
- **Shortcut Option:** In a pinch, replace the homemade meatballs with a 16-to-24 oz bag of fully cooked homestyle frozen beef or turkey meatballs (heated through according to package directions).
